      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T18:08:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PANIC_DATA_FLAG_FRAME_VALID (BIT(0)) was defined specifically to tell host parsers (ectool panicinfo) that pdata-\u003ecm.frame contains a valid  ARM Cortex-M exception stack frame (r0-r3, r12, lr, pc, xpsr). When this flag is not set, these registers are not printed. Should probably be deprecated IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "069c7db0_3990a0d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 46
      },
